## Why This Is Asked
OTA update security for a fleet is a core, tangible skill—tests signing, attestation, rotation, and incident response at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- OTA integrity and authenticity
- Code signing and manifest signing
- Key rotation and revocation
- Secure storage (TEE/SE)
- Incident response for supply-chain events

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code demonstrating verification
const manifestOk = verify(manifest.signature, manifest, publicKey);
if (!manifestOk) fail("manifest bad");
const hashOk = verifyHash(firmware, manifest.hash);
if (!hashOk) fail("hash mismatch");
flashFirmware(firmware);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the OTA signing workflow end-to-end?
- How would you handle devices offline during a rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests handling of edge ID management, data encryption, and strict multitenant data boundaries across cloud services. It requires concrete controls rather than abstractions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge IAM with audience-bound JWTs and gateway introspection
- Envelope encryption and per-tenant key rotation (KMS)
- Snowflake RBAC + Row-Level Security and per-tenant warehouses
- CI/CD secret scanning and misconfiguration checks
- IR playbooks with traceability and forensics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify JWT audience at edge
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function verify(token, expectedAud) {
  try {
    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, KEY, { audience: expectedAud });
    return decoded;
  } catch (e) {
    throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect token reuse across tenants?
- What metrics indicate successful policy enforcement?
